---
import RootModes from "./RootModes.vue";
---

<section id="root" class="section" aria-labelledby="root-title">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">The headline feature</p>
    <h2 id="root-title" class="section-title">Root is a setting, not a weekend project.</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      Choose a root mode when you create a device. Jidr patches its own copy of the image, boots
      it, checks the result and shows a verified badge. Switching back is one click, and the shared
      images in your Android SDK are never modified.
    </p>
    <RootModes client:visible />
    <p class="integrity">
      Rooted emulators can't pass Play Integrity, and no emulator can. Magisk's hiding features only
      affect local root checks.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .integrity {
    margin-top: var(--jidr-space-6);
    padding: var(--jidr-space-3) var(--jidr-space-4);
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--jidr-color-warning);
    background: var(--jidr-color-warning-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--jidr-radius-sm);
    font-size: var(--jidr-text-label);
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
</style>
